cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use egoc-rs in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "egoc-rs: post-quantum commitments with zero-knowledge openings"
abstract: >-
  A Rust library of post-quantum commitment schemes with zero-knowledge
  openings, with two backends: SHADOW-SIS-FIX (a BDLOP commitment over
  module-LWE/MSIS) and EGOC-MCE-R (a matrix-code commitment whose security
  reduces to Matrix Code Equivalence, the problem behind MEDS). The matrix
  encoding is borrowed from Itzhak Bars' two-time physics; the security is not.
authors:
  - family-names: nzengi
    email: zkdaofun@gmail.com
keywords:
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - commitment scheme
  - zero-knowledge proof
  - module-LWE
  - MSIS
  - matrix code equivalence
  - MEDS
  - Rust
license: MIT OR Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-06-02
